The account record and fee schedule reveal a critical issue with the Compass reply. The borrower's most recent courtesy waiver was applied on 2026-09-19, and the late fee was assessed on 2027-10-14—390 days later. According to the fee schedule, a courtesy waiver applies to "one late fee waived in any rolling twelve months (365 days before the fee date)." Since 390 days had elapsed, the borrower was actually eligible for another courtesy waiver within the 365-day rolling window, and the borrower was enrolled in autopay (which qualified them for automatic waivers). 

