The Compass reply stated facts that contradict the account record and fee schedule. The borrower is enrolled in autopay and had their last courtesy waiver applied on 2026-01-15. Since 634 days elapsed before the current late fee assessment on 2027-10-11, the borrower falls outside the rolling 365-day window and is eligible for another courtesy waiver—which should have been applied automatically without requiring a call. The reply incorrectly stated the fee "will remain on your statement" and directed the borrower to call the servicing team, when the fee schedule mandates automatic waiver application for eligible autopay borrowers.

