Based on my review:

**Critical Issue Found**: The Compass reply states "the $25 late fee on your loan ending 8637 will remain on your statement," presenting this as final. However, according to the fee schedule in force (fee-schedule-2026-03), this borrower is eligible for a courtesy waiver: borrowers enrolled in autopay receive one late fee automatically waived within any rolling 365 days. The account record confirms the borrower is enrolled in autopay (since 2024-12-14), and there is no evidence of a prior waived late fee in the preceding 365 days. The reply should have informed the borrower about this waiver eligibility instead of suggesting the fee "will remain" and deflecting to the servicing line. The fee amount ($25) and grace period (15 days) stated are correct, but the waiver status explanation is materially incorrect and misleading.

{"verdict": "fail"}
